WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Air and relative motion. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Define speed and direction relative to air

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Aerodynamic speed is relative to the surrounding air. A crosswind changes the direction and magnitude of that relative flow.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Draw the vehicle velocity and wind vector; subtract vectors to show the air the car actually meets.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Vector sketch

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Define speed and direction relative to air
